#{[1164 #edb/ref 10 :learner-task/remediation-for #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1164 #edb/ref 40 #edb/ref 20 #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1164 #edb/ref 41 #edb/ref 36 #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1164 #edb/ref 62 "Optional references from a review or replacement relearning task to the assessment task(s) whose incorrect, skipped, or unanswered-on-expiration topics triggered required practice. One practice task may address obligations from several assessments. The application matches the task topic to each assessment obligation and clears it only after qualifying successful practice; prior or unrelated practice does not count. These links preserve trigger provenance, are not component ownership, and do not themselves enforce scheduling or record invented wrong answers." #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1165 #edb/ref 10 :learner-task/retake-of #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1165 #edb/ref 40 #edb/ref 20 #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1165 #edb/ref 41 #edb/ref 35 #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1165 #edb/ref 62 "Optional reference from an assessment retake task to the exact original assessment task. This is an attempt relationship, not activity ownership. The application checks assessment task kinds, prevents self/cyclic links and duplicate generated retakes, selects never-presented questions from the original knowledge points, and offers the retake only after required remediation succeeds. The retake remains optional; this relationship alone does not schedule or require it." #edb/ref 13194139534492 #edb/ref 17592186045436]}
